<%# The question asked before an action that cannot be undone at once (log out, delete the account), instead of the
    plain window of the browser: Turbo hands every data-turbo-confirm to confirm_dialog.js, which fills and opens it.
    The question is the title, what follows its question mark on its own line under it, smaller and muted
    (confirm_dialog.js); the confirm button says the action (data-confirm-button of the form or its button,
    "Confirm" otherwise), in red for data-confirm-variant="danger". Both looks are written here in full
    (data-*-classes): no class built from pieces in JavaScript. Escape, Cancel or a click beside it answer no.
    A native <dialog>: the focus stays inside, the page behind is inert.
    tabindex="-1": confirm_dialog.js focuses the window itself, not Cancel, which showed a focus ring at once
    (as in shared/_settings_dialog). Tab then reaches Cancel. No outline on the window: its buttons have their own.
    Like the title bar of the settings window, a line under the question runs from edge to edge. The two buttons
    share the whole width; on a phone they stand one above the other, the action first (flex-col-reverse) %>
<dialog id="confirm-dialog" aria-labelledby="confirm-dialog-question" aria-describedby="confirm-dialog-detail" tabindex="-1"
        class="m-auto w-[min(400px,calc(100vw-2rem))] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-0 text-ink shadow-2xl outline-none backdrop:bg-black/50"
        data-primary-classes="<%= button_classes(:primary, full_width: true) %>"
        data-danger-classes="<%= button_classes(:danger, full_width: true) %>"
        data-default-label="<%= t(".confirm") %>">
  <form method="dialog">
    <div class="border-b border-line px-6 py-4">
      <p id="confirm-dialog-question" class="text-base font-semibold text-ink"></p>
      <p hidden id="confirm-dialog-detail" class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col-reverse gap-3 p-6 sm:flex-row">
      <button type="submit" value="cancel" class="<%= button_classes(:secondary, full_width: true) %>"><%= t(".cancel") %></button>
      <button type="submit" value="confirm" class="<%= button_classes(:primary, full_width: true) %>" data-confirm-dialog-button></button>
    </div>
  </form>
</dialog>
